// Clue Name :
"P3055187448" "Tarixus' Reply"
// DetailString :
"P4015030319" "Tarixus relates that this theoretical 'Arcano-Bomb' is entirely possible, but will require special components. The Legacy Chain is doing study on some unstable magical isotopes in one of their hideouts, and will serve as the explosives for the bomb. Dr. Aeon has developed a design for an energy accelerator that works on magical materials, which will be necessary for activation of the magical isotypes. The accelerator and trigger mechanism itself will require a plethora electronic components. Once these materials are gathered, the Arcano-Bomb can be built."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MagicalIsotopes 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1528897448" "Magical Isotopes"
// DetailString :
"P1788448228" "The stone fragments pulsate with a hypnotizing violet light."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Blueprints 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2366709068" "Energy Accelerator Blueprints"
// DetailString :
"P743448214" "These are blueprints for a high-tech energy accelerator used to initiate chain reactions in potential energy sources. They will be used to cause the magical isotopes to explode in the Arcano-Bomb."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ElectronicsParts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3175151980" "Electronic Parts"
// DetailString :
"P2164111824" "These are various electronics components ripped from the cybernetics of the Freakshow. These will be used for the trigger mechanism of the Arcano-Bomb."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ArcanoBomb 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P543811238" "Arcano-Bomb"
// DetailString :
"P755476359" "This strange-looking device looks like a a series of electronic components, tubes and dials connected by gold and silver wires to a collection of glowing violet rocks. It is a magical bomb made by Archmage Tarixus at the behest of Henri Dumont of the Cage Consortium."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeOneClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4263934175" "Off to see the Wizard"
// DetailString :
"P1118639978" "It all started when Henri Dumont revealed the Cage Consortium discovered a vein of bauxite under Potter's Field. The problem was that Potter's Field was a cemetary where the local workers buried their dead, and starting to mine their would be a PR nightmare unless handled properly. Henri came up with a plan to set off a magical bomb that would expose the bauxite vein while pointing a finger towards the Circle of Thorns as the responsible party. You were sent to discuss the plan with Archmage Tarixus, who came up with the necessary components to create this 'Arcano-Bomb'."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeTwoClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2056510914" "Magical Rocks"
// DetailString :
"P3560992635" "It all started when Henri Dumont revealed the Cage Consortium discovered a vein of bauxite under Potter's Field. The problem was that Potter's Field was a cemetary where the local workers buried their dead, and starting to mine their would be a PR nightmare unless handled properly. Henri came up with a plan to set off a magical bomb that would expose the bauxite vein while pointing a finger towards the Circle of Thorns as the responsible party. You were sent to discuss the plan with Archmage Tarixus, who came up with the necessary components to create this 'Arcano-Bomb'.<br><br>The first objective was to obtain unstable magical isotopes that the Legacy Chain were studying in one of their hideouts on the Rogue Isles. After a successful raid on the hideout, you acquired the explosive components for the bomb."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeThreeClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P416985050" "Raiding Dr. Aeon"
// DetailString :
"P3129652920" "It all started when Henri Dumont revealed the Cage Consortium discovered a vein of bauxite under Potter's Field. The problem was that Potter's Field was a cemetary where the local workers buried their dead, and starting to mine their would be a PR nightmare unless handled properly. Henri came up with a plan to set off a magical bomb that would expose the bauxite vein while pointing a finger towards the Circle of Thorns as the responsible party. You were sent to discuss the plan with Archmage Tarixus, who came up with the necessary components to create this 'Arcano-Bomb'.<br><br>The first objective was to obtain unstable magical isotopes that the Legacy Chain were studying in one of their hideouts on the Rogue Isles. After a successful raid on the hideout, you acquired the explosive components for the bomb.<br><br>The next objective was to gather electronics components for the trigger mechanism. Since the Cage Consortium has been having problems with the Freakshow raiding their facilities, Henri thought it would be best to take out two birds with one stone. He sent you to take down and rip the electronics components from Freakshow cybernetic implants. You accomplished this task and returned the components to Henri."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeFourClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P189685046" "Ripping apart the Freakshow"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeFiveClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2694146857" "Constructing the Arcano-Bomb"
// DetailString :
"P1853329825" "It all started when Henri Dumont revealed the Cage Consortium discovered a vein of bauxite under Potter's Field. The problem was that Potter's Field was a cemetary where the local workers buried their dead, and starting to mine their would be a PR nightmare unless handled properly. Henri came up with a plan to set off a magical bomb that would expose the bauxite vein while pointing a finger towards the Circle of Thorns as the responsible party. You were sent to discuss the plan with Archmage Tarixus, who came up with the necessary components to create this 'Arcano-Bomb'.<br><br>The first objective was to obtain unstable magical isotopes that the Legacy Chain were studying in one of their hideouts on the Rogue Isles. After a successful raid on the hideout, you acquired the explosive components for the bomb.<br><br>The next objective was to gather electronics components for the trigger mechanism. Since the Cage Consortium has been having problems with the Freakshow raiding their facilities, Henri thought it would be best to take out two birds with one stone. He sent you to take down and rip the electronics components from Freakshow cybernetic implants. You accomplished this task and returned the components to Henri.<br><br>Henri directed you to take the components to Tarixus.  With a twirl of magical energy he created the Arcano-Bomb!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SouvenirDepletedMagicIsotope 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3279974055" "Depleted Magical Isotope"
// tDetailString :
"P2055137136" "This is a depleted magical isotope you collected from a tale you like to call:<br><br>Disturbing the Dead<br><br>It all started when Henri Dumont revealed the Cage Consortium discovered a vein of bauxite under Potter's Field. The problem was that Potter's Field was a cemetary where the local workers buried their dead, and starting to mine their would be a PR nightmare unless handled properly. Henri came up with a plan to set off a magical bomb that would expose the bauxite vein while pointing a finger towards the Circle of Thorns as the responsible party. You were sent to discuss the plan with Archmage Tarixus, who came up with the necessary components to create this 'Arcano-Bomb'.<br><br>The first objective was to obtain unstable magical isotopes that the Legacy Chain were studying in one of their hideouts on the Rogue Isles. After a successful raid on the hideout, you acquired the explosive components for the bomb.<br><br>The next objective was to gather electronics components for the trigger mechanism. Since the Cage Consortium has been having problems with the Freakshow raiding their facilities, Henri thought it would be best to take out two birds with one stone. He sent you to take down and rip the electronics components from Freakshow cybernetic implants. You accomplished this task and returned the components to Henri.<br><br>Henri directed you to take the components to Tarixus.  With a twirl of magical energy he created the Arcano-Bomb!<br><br>Taking the Arcano-Bomb, you planted it in a Circle of Thorns temple deep underneath Potter's Field. After escaping the lair, Henri set it off - only to find that it only affected the spirit-world! While it took down a number of Circle of Thorns, it did nothing to the actual land that made up Potter's Field. It turns out Tarixus had other ideas which did not involve the welfare of the Cage Consortium."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission_1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2825589993" "Sharkhead Isle has been very good to the Cage Consortium in terms of exploitable natural resources. The bauxite deposits have provided years of good strip-mining production, which has in turn made the company a lot of money. But we realize that these deposits aren't infinite, so need to start looking to the future. In order to protect the interests of the workers that bring us the big bucks, we need to start looking for more readily available bauxite deposits.<br><br>Some of our surveyors have discovered that Potter's Field has a rather rich deposit of bauxite. Unfortunately, due to the unfortunate proximity of the graveyard, exposing the bauxite deposits via blasting might result in some bad PR for the Consortium. So we'd like to do some 'creative social engineering', setting up a scapegoat to take the blame for the explosion, while the Cage Consortium steps in and gives the workers a pittance to make it look like we care, all the while setting up operations to start mining the exposed vein. Tres bien, non?<br><br>I know someone who can help us with this little problem, an individual known as Archmage Tarixus. He has claimed a portion of Potter's Field for himself, and has little care for the Circle of Thorns there. If we can convince him to help us make a magical bomb to use on a part of Potter's Field and the Circle of Thorns will take the blame! <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Head over to Potter's Field and speak with Archmage Tarixus</A>."
// AcceptString :
"P3805450790" "Speak to Archmage Tarixus"
// SendOffString :
"P1424070680" "Tarixus should be able to provide you with the necessary components for this magical bomb."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1028166813" "We're on a clock here, {VillainName}, and you don't get paid for overtime. Talk with Tarixus, rapidement!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2184911364" "Hrm, yes. This 'Arcano-Bomb' is entirely possible, but will require special components. From my divinations, I know the Legacy Chain is doing study on some unstable magical isotopes in one of their hideouts, and will serve as the explosives for the bomb. Dr. Aeon has developed a design for an energy accelerator that works on magical materials, which will be necessary for activation of the magical isotypes. The accelerator and trigger mechanism itself will require a plethora of electronic components. Once these materials are gathered, the Arcano-Bomb can be built!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2172776509" "This is what is required, eh? Well we should get started on this right away!"
